{
  "context_id": "4kxv-chain-a-p29401",
  "limits": [
    "The article directly identifies its human transketolase QM/MM model as derived from PDB 4KXV and names chain-A Lys244 and His258, while the PDB and PDBe mappings establish chain A as UniProt P29401 at those positions.",
    "The article predicts protonation and acid-base behavior computationally and cites yeast mutagenesis as motivation; this projection makes no experimentally established catalytic-role, protonation-state, pKa, transition-state, or complete-mechanism claim.",
    "This proposal-specific human context does not apply mechanism 1 or its 1TRK/P23254 yeast residue rows to P29401.",
    "The paper supports the textual X5P plus E4P to F6P plus G3P context for its human study, but the M-CSA mechanism-2 MRV drawings retain CHEBI:57483 (S7P) identifier labels on sugar atoms. This projection does not resolve, relabel, or atom-map that source conflict and does not assert a canonical balanced reaction instance.",
    "The retained 4KXV mmCIF is current revision 2.1 dated 2023-09-20, after the 2020 computational paper. It supports current deposited identity and mapping but is not claimed to be byte-identical to the coordinate file used by the paper.",
    "The 4KXV construct has 637 polymer positions; the deposited P29401 alignment covers positions 1-623 and identifies positions 624-637 as an expression tag. Construct length is not treated as UniProt length."
  ],
